# Deterministic fuse check for the print-in-place chain. Like the piano
# hinge, there is no flexure web to excuse: the 11 links are joined only
# through clearances, so a healthy run is ELEVEN disjoint shells in the
# sliced STL and no flexure zone needs dropping — count them directly. A
# stub welded into its bore (clear_xy lost) or a lug welded to an ear
# (side_gap lost) reads as fewer bodies: a STRONG WARN for reviewer signoff.
assert pip-cable-chain.stl 11

# Mandatory negative control: part="fused" drives oversized stubs through
# every bore, welding the run into one solid. It must STAY one body —
# proving the check can fire (and that no over-generous zone is masking a
# real fuse by splitting the control too).
control fused 1
